  "derivation": "Same as export.prepare.repairable-pre-normalize but the declared recipe assoc-direction-fix selects nothing (its where is false), so N leaves Assoc_1 unchanged. DESIGN \u00a76.2: 'a repairable pre-N error may continue only with its declared bounded repair recipe; post-N unresolved errors block'; \u00a76.4: 'corrected pre-N findings remain history with disposition corrected'. The rule assoc-direction (phase pre-normalize, classification repairable, repairRecipe assoc-direction-fix, accept severity error) finds Assoc_1 without associationDirection. The pre-normalize stage continues (a recipe is declared), N reports no change, the post-normalize lint finds nothing new, and the pre-N finding was not corrected: it is an unresolved error after N, so preparation refuses with its code association-direction-missing at the post-normalize stage (first unresolved error entry, harmonization C19); the report keeps the finding with disposition observed. Options are validated before the pipeline (closed option record, format declared with a registered adapter, theme resolvable; harmonization C18); then each stage runs exactly once on a staged deep copy in the DESIGN \u00a710.2 order compatibility -> graph checks -> C -> pre-normalize -> N -> post-normalize -> layout -> post-layout -> release -> R -> map under the accept policy, edit activation; the sealed trace lists the stages the observer saw, in order. A refusal returns the complete report of the executed lint stages (no change entry, no candidate) and no artifact (harmonization B2); no input is mutated.",
